From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:41:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: nn::audio is mixed and played (voices, ADPCM,
 sink, audio out), save data has a journal (commit and rollback), movie
 openings are refused explicitly

horizon_audio mixes the voices into buses and the sink's channels through libnx2linux_audio.so (SDL3 device, WAV file or nothing); ADPCM is decoded when a buffer is queued. horizon_fs: SaveDir keeps a working copy and commits atomically, with Commit, Unmount and restart semantics of the console, plus rename, set size, delete directory, free space, more mount overloads. horizon_movie: the SDK's Extractor openings fail with its own no-implementation code, counted and named, instead of a decoder that answers 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: NX2Linux milestone E: the game's audio is played, its saves are written with commit and rollback, and a movie it cannot play fails explicitly
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch Téo/jalon-e-audio-saves-video)

